The Rhythm: Canonical Sequences
Your point about "after much sun comes a summer storm" is the convective cycle. On a hot summer day, the sun heats the ground, warm air rises (thermal), cumulus clouds build, and by 4-6 PM — if there's enough moisture and instability — a thunderstorm breaks out.
This is a multi-day sequence with a specific temporal structure:
SUMMER CONVECTIVE CYCLE (2-3 days):
  Day 1: clear_morning → cumulus_humilis (small puffy clouds, 11am) 
         → cumulus_mediocris (taller, 2pm) → cumulus_congestus (towering, 4pm)
         → thunderstorms (5-7pm) → gust_front → clearing_by_night
  Day 2: residual_moisture → partly_cloudy → possible_afternoon_shower (weaker)
  Day 3: stable_clearing → sunny_dry
WINTER ANTICYCLONIC FOG CYCLE (3-10 days):
  Day 1: high_pressure_settles → radiation_fog_overnight → fog_until_11am → 
         thin_sun → fog_returns_by_5pm
  Day 2: same_pattern (slightly denser fog, takes longer to burn off)
  Day 3-5: persistent_stratus — fog NEVER clears, temp stays 0-3°C all day
  Day 6: weak_front_approaches → wind picks up → fog_dissipates → overcast_drizzle
  
  This can persist for 10+ days in valleys (Po Valley, Central Europe basins).
  The key insight: day 4 of a fog event is DIFFERENT from day 1.
  Day 1: might clear. Day 4: won't clear. Duration changes the probabilities.
MID-LATITUDE CYCLONE (3-5 days, any season):
  Phase 1 (approach): high_cirrus → lowering_stratus → pressure_falling 
  Phase 2 (warm front): steady_rain → temperature_rising → wind_backing_SW
  Phase 3 (warm sector): mild_humid → drizzle_or_clear → pressure_stable
  Phase 4 (cold front): sudden_wind_shift → heavy_rain_squall → temperature_drop 
  Phase 5 (clearing): rapid_clearing → cold_bright → pressure_rising
These are irreversible sequences — the system moves through phases in order. A cold front doesn't go backwards into a warm sector. This is why the Markov needs order > 1: knowing only "today = Phase 3 (warm sector)" gives P(rain tomorrow). But knowing "(Phase 2, Phase 3)" tells you it's likely advancing to Phase 4 — that information is in the pair, not the single state.
